            <ArticleTitle>Idiopathic carotid and coronary vasospasm: a new syndrome?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>273-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1552-6569.2009.00460.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the first case of cerebral infarction due to idiopathic reversible vasospasm of the extracranial internal carotid artery without headache or identifiable cause in a patient who subsequently suffered acute myocardial infarction due to vasospasm of the coronary artery.</AbstractText>
